#. Diagram label
msgid "document only"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:153
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Does this agreement carry a machine-readable ODRL 2.2 Agreement beside its text? `yes` derives it and has it checked; `document only` goes straight on (a signed PDF is a valid agreement)."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:225
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Each signed version gets its own immutable URL (for example /dsa/42/v3). A 'latest' URL may exist; nothing cites it. A new version never overwrites an old one."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:379
#. Diagram label
msgid "end"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:314
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Existing grants keep citing the old hash. The parties decide, per agreement: they stay valid until expiry, or they are revoked and reissued against the new version (in smart-trust). The old version stays readable."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:99
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Gives each signed version its own immutable URL, records its SHA-256 hash, and writes the DCAT 3 catalogue record. Also sets the catalogue status when the agreement ends."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:41
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "How a data sharing agreement is drafted, negotiated, signed, published with a version, a hash and a catalogue record, and later amended, renewed or ended. It covers the agreement as a document folio only: processes P1, P2 and P14 of the DSA process catalogue. Two entry points: a request for an agreement (P1, then P2), and a change to one in force (P14). An amendment or a renewal with a new end date runs P1 and P2 again and publishes a new version linked to the old one; the old version stays readable. Standards named: ODRL 2.2 (the Agreement), DCAT 3 (catalogue record, distributions, checksums, versions) and DCMI Terms (dcterms:source from the policy to the text). No field is defined here. Steps no skill covers yet are user tasks with a no-skill reason starting \"Gap:\". Owner's option B13-B, 2026-10-30; folio-assistant#2702."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:237
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Is there an ODRL Agreement for this version? `yes`: it must cite the text by URL and hash. `document only`: go straight to publishing."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:183
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Legal and policy review of the whole draft. Reviewers comment on blocks through review-comments; review says which review skill answers which question."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:249
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Merge: the computable and document-only paths meet before the version is published."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:171
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Merge: the computable and the document-only paths meet before the text is split into public terms and private annexes."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:140
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Merge: the first draft, a review that asks for changes, and an amendment or renewal (P14) all come back to writing the text."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:201
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Merge: with or without public comment, the reviewers then decide whether the draft is ready to sign."
msgstr ""

