msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:320
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Set the life-cycle status of the agreement's DCAT 3 record (DCAT 3 §6.4.30). The published versions stay readable at their URLs."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:189
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Should the public template go out for public comment before signing? `yes` runs Process_PublicComment; `no` goes straight to the readiness decision. A private agreement between two parties usually answers `no`."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:130
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Someone else holds the bean; this run stops without touching it."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:177
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Split the agreement into a public template and private annexes (security controls, named staff). Only the hash of a private annex is ever published."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:276
#. Diagram label
msgid "Terms change, end date reached, or notice given"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:338
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The agreement has expired or been terminated, its catalogue status says so, and its versions stay readable."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:52
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The data provider and the data recipient (ODRL 2.2 assigner and assignee) and the people who sign for them. Their role is judgement only: they agree the terms, sign, and decide whether to amend, renew or end the agreement. No skill can make those choices for them, so no activity in this lane names one."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:243
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The ODRL policy names the signed text distribution with dcterms:source (DCMI Terms), pointing at the immutable URL whose spdx:checksum was just recorded."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:134
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The parties agree the purpose, the datasets, the period, the conditions and duties, and which trust anchors each side accepts. This sets what the text must say; it is a negotiation between people."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:297
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The parties decide what happens to the agreement. Deciding to amend or terminate is human; expiry of a computable agreement is already enforced by its ODRL dateTime constraint."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:303
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The parties' decision. `new version` (amend, or renew with a new end date) runs P1 again and publishes a new version linked to the old one. `renew by grant` (the version has no end date): nothing in the document changes. `end` (expiry or termination) closes the agreement."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:207
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The reviewers' call. `changes needed` sends the draft back to the author; `ready` renders it for signing."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:219
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The signatories sign: wet ink, or an electronic signature under national law. Technically a detached JWS (RFC 7515) or CMS (RFC 5652); PAdES for a signed PDF needs the owner's approval."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:273
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The signed version is at its immutable URL, with its hash and catalogue record. Grants and keys that cite it are issued in the server processes (smart-trust), not here."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:310
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The version has no end date, so renewal is a new grant under the same version. Grants are issued in the server processes (smart-trust), not here."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:95
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Used only when the public part of the agreement (the template) goes out for public comment. Comments are handled in Process_PublicComment, the same as for any document folio."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:272
#. Diagram label
msgid "Version published — agreement in force"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:63
#. Diagram label
msgid "Work plan — beans (shared by humans and agents)"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:147
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Write the agreement as a document folio: one normative statement per clause the parties must keep, through normative-statements. The text says which governs if it and a machine-readable form disagree (suggested: the text)."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:77
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Writes the legal text and, for a computable agreement, derives the ODRL 2.2 Agreement from it. Every loop comes back here: a review that asks for changes, an amendment, and a renewal that needs a new version."
msgstr ""

